{
 "about": "3-D FDTD ringdowns of a dielectric brick on an infinite ground plane, from otahub.num.dra.brick. eps = relative permittivity; A = length along the magnetic dipole / height; B = width across it / height; cells = grid cells per height; k0d = k0*height at resonance; Q = Re/(2 Im) of the complex frequency. Air margin 14 cells, CPML 12 cells, float32. 'train' is what the rectangular_dra fits were made from; 'test' was held out: other permittivities, aspect ratios off the training grid, and three points re-run on a finer grid. Where the loudest mode at the probe was a higher-order one (long narrow bars), the point was re-run taking the lowest mode with real amplitude, which is what the module does now.",
